# Paper report style (global)

When creating **documentation** (Markdown, HTML, Canvas, briefings, styled analytical pages), apply the **paper-report-style** visual system (fonts, palette, layout chrome only).

Skill: `~/.cursor/skills/paper-report-style/` (`SKILL.md`, `paper-base.css`, `reference.md`).

## Must use

- Fonts (where controllable): **Archivo** · **IBM Plex Sans** · **IBM Plex Mono**
- Tokens: paper `#EFF2F1`, ink `#141A1C`, accent `#C2661B`, rel `#0E8F73`, fleet `#3A6FD8`, block `#9C3587` (+ dark)
- Chrome: eyebrow → title → thesis → optional KPI band → numbered sections → callout/ledger/decision; hairlines; 2–4px radius when CSS applies

Does **not** dictate document content. Does **not** override product app UI unless asked. Not HTML-only.
